{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Citation-only judge version: closed id lists in the answer format (design v2, D712)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Alex's decision (D712, 2026-11-21):** \"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\". The question offered: every id field of the judge's answer takes\n     4\ta closed list built from the request; a $0 check on stored data that accepted answers still pass and the bad ids are excluded; any\n     5\tpaid test asks him again.\n     6\t\n     7\t**Scope:** the answer format's four id fields, and the checks needed to enforce them:\n     8\t- the local validator's `maxItems`;\n     9\t- preflight reading each call's saved format.\n    10\t\n    11\t**Not changed:**\n    12\t- the prompt text;\n    13\t- the request text;\n    14\t- the rung field;\n    15\t- `check_answer` and its retry;\n    16\t- any retry policy;\n    17\t- what evidence is shown;\n    18\t- the link direction (a separate design, D711).\n    19\t\n    20\tv2 answers council round 38 (`codex-r38.md`): the format-error path, the batch and resume cells, duplicate theme pushes, preflight,\n    21\tthe D358 sizes, lists from the rendered rows, an unused version name, and the T1 proof.\n    22\t\n    23\t## 1. Census (stored data, $0)\n    24\t\n    25\t- **Refusals.** Every refused judge answer on the stored runs is an id-membership error: an id outside the list its field allows.\n    26\t  - Population (Codex r37b and r38, reproduced by Claude's `id_typo_census.py`): 5,415 archive rows, 5,408 distinct request-answer\n    27\t    pairs, 5,389 committed, 17 refused, 2 valid answers of the stopped control batch never committed. Sources: old-1, old-2, old-3,\n    28\t    and the pilots' fresh rows.\n    29\t  - The classes:\n    30\t    - a one-character copy of a listed evidence id (e3620 → e362);\n    31\t    - a garbled evidence id (`e393`);\n    32\t    - a theme id in `cites_views` or in an evidence field;\n    33\t    - a dependency id used as an evidence id.\n    34\t- **The same class halted a run before (D358, 2026-10-28).** The sealed three-month run's Data Center request showed 698 evidence\n    35\t  ids; \"the model mislabels one id among dozens of pushes about every other attempt, the code refuses the answer, two refusals halt\n    36\t  the day\".\n    37\t- **List sizes per request**, counting evidence twice (cites and push ids) plus themes, dependencies and the two 3-value push enums:\n    38\t  - the five archives: max 915 (old-1 call 5652: 451 evidence ids);\n    39\t  - the sealed D358 archive: 10 of 949 requests over 1,000; call 6918 has 647 evidence ids, which is 1,323 values as plain enums and\n    40\t    676 if one shared evidence enum counts once.\n    41\t- **Provider limits** (OpenAI structured outputs guide, read 2026-11-21):\n    42\t  - \"up to 1000 enum values across all enum properties\";\n    43\t  - above 250 values, at most 15,000 characters per string enum;\n    44\t  - 120,000 characters in all;\n    45\t  - `minItems`/`maxItems` and `$defs`/`$ref` are supported;\n    46\t  - the guide is silent on empty enums and on how a referenced enum counts.\n    47\t\n    48\t## 2. Mechanism\n    49\t\n    50\tEvery request's closing line already forbids the wrong ids (`judging.py` lines 180–182). The answer format accepts any string there\n    51\t(`schema_for`, lines 55–75), so the model breaks the prose rule: about 0.3% of answers, 2.6% of linked readers', and every other\n    52\tattempt on a 698-id request (D358).\n    53\t\n    54\tThe code already decides membership after the answer (`check_answer`). Moving the same set into the format makes a wrong id\n    55\tunwritable: code owns identity (AGENTS §2). The judge still decides which evidence matters and how it pushes.\n    56\t\n    57\t## 3. The change\n    58\t\n    59\t- **One new version, `judging-v12`** (unused name; `judging-v9` named an earlier experiment):\n    60\t  - It has judging-v7's text and request, with closed lists. Its prompt file is a byte copy pinned to v7's sha.\n    61\t  - `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` gains it. `schema_for('judging-v7')` and `schema_for('judging-v8')` keep `JUDGING_SCHEMA_SHA`.\n    62\t  - Config: `poc-v121` = poc-v118 with `rejudging.prompt_version` = judging-v12.\n    63\t  - No v8-based version is built. The shared list builder is proven on linked-1's saved v8 requests offline (T2).\n    64\t- **The lists come from the rows that render the request**, not from parsing its text:\n    65\t  - one function returns the system text, the user text and the three id lists from the same objects at the same store state:\n    66\t    - evidence: the `pieces` it prints;\n    67\t    - dependencies: the resolved dependencies that get an entry (a waiting dependency has no citable target);\n    68\t    - themes: the themes it prints;\n    69\t  - `build_prompt` keeps its signature and returns the first two;\n    70\t  - `round_of_judgements` builds each view's schema from the lists, and `ask` sends it, the retry included;\n    71\t  - this matches `check_answer`'s sets at the same state, and is not fooled by an id inside a multiline quote or reasons (Codex r38\n    72\t    counterexamples).\n    73\t- **The format.**\n    74\t  - One `$defs` string enum of the evidence ids, sorted, referenced by `cites.items` and `pushes.items.evidence_id`.\n    75\t  - A plain enum of the dependency ids for `cites_views.items`.\n    76\t  - A plain enum of the theme ids for `theme_pushes.items.view_id`.\n    77\t  - An empty list gives its array `maxItems: 0` with items `{\"type\": \"string\"}`; no empty enum is written.\n    78\t  - The schema name stays `judgement`.\n    79\t- **The local validator** (`model.check_schema`) gains `maxItems`, the mirror of `minItems`. No existing schema uses it (grep), so\n    80\t  no current answer changes status.\n    81\t- **Preflight part A** checks each stored refused row against the format saved in that row's own request\n    82\t  (`request_json.response_format.json_schema.schema`), not against a fixed per-purpose schema. For every existing row this is the\n    83\t  same schema that was sent; a test shows equal tallies on old-2's archive.\n    84\t- **Size.**\n    85\t  - No pre-send counting rule: the provider's counting of a referenced enum is unverified, and a guessed rule could refuse a\n    86\t    request the provider accepts.\n    87\t  - A request the provider refuses comes back as HTTP 400, which the transport raises at once without retrying (`openai_transport`).\n    88\t    It goes through `judge_day`'s generic path to `judging_failed`, and the day is resumable. A resume sends the same oversized\n    89\t    request and hits the same limit; that visible stop is the behaviour until a design change.\n    90\t  - No rule drops evidence to fit.\n    91\t\n    92\t## 4. Tables\n    93\t\n    94\t### 4.1 State × event\n    95\t\n    96\t| State / event | What happens | What is written; which date |\n    97\t|---|---|---|\n    98\t| First judgement | the lists are built as for any request | as now |\n    99\t| No dependency (all of poc-v121) | `cites_views` has `maxItems: 0` | — |\n   100\t| No theme | `theme_pushes` has `maxItems: 0` | — |\n   101\t| No evidence printed | `cites` and `pushes` have `maxItems: 0` (eligible views have evidence in force, but the printed set can be empty) | — |\n   102\t| A membership error from the provider (should not occur under strict mode) | `model.check_schema` refuses it: the row is saved with `:schema:`, `SchemaError` is raised, and the error reaches `judge_day`'s generic `judging_failed` path (not `judgement_refused_twice`, and no retry) | the refused row, suffixed; the day is resumable; a resume re-samples |\n   103\t| A `check_answer` refusal not about membership (rung range, a rung move without changed, an empty stance, a duplicate theme push) | the retry carries the same schema; a second refusal → `judgement_refused_twice` | as now |\n   104\t| Several workers in a level, one fails | other workers' answers may already be saved, while the level records no judgement; on resume, committed judgements are skipped and saved answers are reused when the rebuilt request is byte-equal | as now |\n   105\t| Resume after a config or input change | a different request means a new key and a fresh answer | as now |\n   106\t| A theme closes, or a dependency resolves, after the request is built | the lists are frozen in the sent format; `check_answer` reads the sent text for evidence and themes, and the store for dependencies, which cannot resolve during judging (it resolves in writing) | — |\n   107\t| The provider refuses the format (HTTP 400: size or keyword) | not retried by the transport → `judging_failed` → resumable; a resume hits the same limit | no answer row |\n   108\t| A valid id that names the wrong source | not detectable by code | measured separately (§6) |\n   109\t\n   110\t### 4.2 Value × reader\n   111\t\n   112\t| Value | Reader | Effect |\n   113\t|---|---|---|\n   114\t| The per-request schema | `model.build_request`, then `request_identity` (archive key) | every v12 judge request has a new key: no stored answer is reused; any paired run needs its own replay proof |\n   115\t| The schema name `judgement` | `paid_run.is_judgement_request`, `july_test` | unchanged |\n   116\t| The saved format | preflight part A | read per row (changed, above) |\n   117\t| The answer | `vocabulary.judgement_answer`, `_record` | the same shape |\n   118\t| The input size | cost | about 450 characters at the median, up to about 3,700 at the five archives' max with the shared enum; priced at $0.10 per million input tokens; measured in the $0 test |\n   119\t\n   120\t### 4.3 New path × old checks\n   121\t\n   122\t| Old check | Under v12 |\n   123\t|---|---|\n   124\t| `check_answer` membership | still runs; it cannot fire on an answer that passed the format |\n   125\t| Rung range, first-judgement changed, rung move needs changed, stance non-empty, duplicate theme push | unchanged |\n   126\t| Frozen tests | v7/v8 unchanged; v12's prompt sha = v7's; a pinned schema on a fixed list |\n   127\t| D359 (only named versions are built) | `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` gains `judging-v12` only |\n   128\t| Launchers | poc-v121 is a product config like poc-v118 |\n   129\t\n   130\t### 4.4 Prior decisions\n   131\t\n   132\t- D354 and D712: the frozen judge, now opened by Alex.\n   133\t- D359: the code builds only named versions.\n   134\t- D694: a new name for a request change.\n   135\t- D198: the closed set is what the request showed.\n   136\t- D358: the evidence-bloat halts, the same class.\n   137\t- D711: the census and the recommendation.\n   138\t- The pre-v74i extraction admission schema constrained `folds_into` to the shown ids. It was removed with the frozen prompt (commit\n   139\t  248ef1b4); no decision rejected it.\n   140\t\n   141\t## 5. The $0 test (registered before it runs)\n   142\t\n   143\t### T1: the product path\n   144\told-2 is replayed under poc-v121 with the existing replay runner.\n   145\t- **The transport.** It finds each judge request's stored old-2 call by its (system, user) bytes; the 1,620 pairs are unique (Codex\n   146\t  r38). It asserts that the rest of the outgoing request equals the stored one except the format. It returns the stored answer, which\n   147\t  then goes through the real `model.call` and `model.check_schema`.\n   148\t- **The four refused first calls** (e88, e3955, e3998, theme ids). The first request gets the saved accepted retry answer, a\n   149\t  labelled substitution: under strict mode the provider could not have returned the refused one.\n   150\t- **Pass.**\n   151\t  - The replay completes, and the store equals old-2's on every table and on every substantive judgement field, including both push\n   152\t    lists and `why_changed`.\n   153\t  - New request hashes and the config are recorded and checked apart.\n   154\t  - Every judge answer passed the real validator.\n   155\t\n   156\t### T1b: the four originals\n   157\tEach refused original goes through the real `model.call` under its v12 request and raises `SchemaError` on the id `check_answer`\n   158\trefused.\n   159\t\n   160\t### T2: every stored shape, offline\n   161\t- For every stored judge request of old-1, old-2, old-3, control-1 and linked-1, the lists are taken from the saved text. These are\n   162\t  archived calls whose store state is gone; a text parser can only widen a list, so it can only make this test easier, never\n   163\t  harder, and T1 covers the built path.\n   164\t- Each answer is validated through the real `check_schema` with the v12 format.\n   165\t- Pass:\n   166\t  - all 5,389 committed answers and the 2 uncommitted valid ones validate;\n   167\t  - all 17 refused answers fail on their bad id;\n   168\t  - the population is printed as in §1.\n   169\t\n   170\t### T3: the real validator's controls\n   171\tFor all four fields, through `model.check_schema`:\n   172\t- an allowed id passes;\n   173\t- an unlisted id fails;\n   174\t- an empty list with `maxItems: 0` passes `[]` and fails `[\"v1\"]`.\n   175\t\n   176\tT3 fails on today's validator, which ignores `maxItems`.\n   177\t\n   178\t### T4: sizes\n   179\tThe largest format over the five archives and over the sealed D358 archive is printed: evidence count, enum values with the\n   180\treference counted once and counted twice, and characters.\n   181\t\n   182\t### Mutants\n   183\tEach is caught by a test that passes on the unmutated code:\n   184\t- push ids left open;\n   185\t- lists parsed from the text instead of taken from the rows (the multiline-quote case);\n   186\t- `maxItems` dropped for an empty list;\n   187\t- `maxItems` removed from the validator;\n   188\t- preflight reading the fixed schema.\n   189\t\n   190\t### Also\n   191\t- Prompt size: the format's characters and tokens before and after, median and max.\n   192\t- The suite, the frozen tests and `docs/check.py`.\n   193\t\n   194\t## 6. What the $0 test cannot show\n   195\t\n   196\t- **Provider acceptance of the exact format:** the shared reference, `maxItems: 0`, and a largest request (D358 call 6918's size).\n   197\t- **Whether the judge picks the intended source when constrained:** e3111 could become e3110 or e3112.\n   198\t- **Whether the forecasts move.**\n   199\t\n   200\tA paid step, Alex's to open, settles these. It would first send the largest stored request and an empty-list request to check\n   201\tacceptance, then re-send the stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones, and read the cited sources beside the\n   202\tforecasts.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/lchingen/.codex/skills/codex-claude-council/SKILL.md; rg -n '\"'^## D71[12]|''^## D358|''^### 7.1'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md AGENTS.md; tail -3 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md | cut -c1-280; rg -n '\"'^#|D712'\"' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | tail -22\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat /Users/lchingen/.codex/skills/codex-claude-council/SKILL.md; rg -n '\"'^## D71[12]|''^## D358|''^### 7.1'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md AGENTS.md; tail -3 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md | cut -c1-280; rg -n '\"'^#|D712'\"' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | tail -22\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: codex-claude-council\ndescription: Run a multi-round research and challenge council between Codex and Claude Code on a specified objective, seeking evidence-backed agreement while preserving genuine disagreements. Use when the user requests a joint council, debate, or iterative co-review with Claude Code.\n---\n\n# Codex and Claude Code council\n\nClarify the objective, scope, constraints, evidence and decision needed from the request and workspace. Apply the repository's instructions and existing authorization; a council does not authorize unrelated changes or override a user's decisions. State what each reviewer must leave out of scope.\n\n## Independent investigation\n\n- Codex investigates the primary sources, code and relevant prior decisions itself. Give Claude Code the same objective, scope and primary materials, but avoid supplying a preferred conclusion in its initial assignment where independence matters. Ask it to cite exact files and concrete evidence, distinguish facts from hypotheses, and propose the cheapest decisive checks and counterexamples.\n- Run Claude Code with the model the user chose or, if none, an available appropriate model. For read-only review restrict tools to `Read,Glob,Grep` and a read-only permission mode. Preserve the exact handoff, session ID, streaming output and terminal result in the task's work area. Never bypass permissions.\n- A typical local invocation is `claude -p --model <model> --permission-mode plan --tools Read,Glob,Grep --output-format stream-json --verbose < handoff.txt > round-1.jsonl 2> round-1.stderr`. Validate installed CLI options first. Continue the same session using `--resume <session-id>` with the next challenge. Check final result and exit status; tool activity or a partial stream is not completion. Poll the running process and surface meaningful progress; do not kill a working reviewer merely because it is taking minutes. Report actual failures or access limitations accurately.\n\n## Challenge and converge\n\nCompare independent findings against the underlying material yourself before presenting them as established. Send Claude the specific disagreements, counterexamples and your own analysis, and ask it to challenge its prior conclusions as well as yours. Repeat until each material claim and proposed next step is explicitly agreed with its supporting evidence, or the remaining uncertainty or disagreement is identified. Agreement is not proof: identify what would falsify the shared hypothesis and which claims remain untested. Do not force consensus or invent a reviewer response.\n\nKeep rounds proportionate and purposeful. A reviewer who is still investigating should be allowed to finish. If meaningful progress stops because of an actual failure or impasse, preserve the trace and tell the user what remains unresolved.\n\n## Deliver\n\nGive the user the conclusion in plain language, concrete source examples, agreed causes versus hypotheses, unresolved disagreements, priority and the next discriminating test. Preserve the exchange and a concise decision record where the task's existing documentation belongs. Update dependent human-readable views when the workspace requires it. Implement changes only within the user's authorized scope and after the applicable project diagnosis and review requirements; do not change frozen baselines or treat the council's agreement as approval for a new product decision.\nAGENTS.md:239:### 7.1 The ruler\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3783:## D358 · 2026-10-28 (carried 2026-11-04) · The three-month run stops at 2026-08-28 and is sealed; evidence bloat is the next problem to solve\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10660:## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10689:## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 A\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n1:# Current state\n103:## Future evidence scoring (D372)\n107:## Latest decision (D369)\n128:## What runs\n140:## Open defects\n159:## One next task\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
