{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; sed -n '239,290p' AGENTS.md; sed -n '10660,10707p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; sed -n '239,290p' AGENTS.md; sed -n '10660,10707p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\n  nothing at all and were never judged.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n| Evidence | Content | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Filing recognises only \"its own figure\" | The model says \"Broadcom's AI chip revenue is not cloud providers' spending on custom chips\" and \"Google Cloud's backlog is not capital spending\"; on a neutral refiling (no question id named, the rule not shown), 23 of 42 facts that matter are still not filed | `probe-filing-account-d1.md`, `refile-no_fallback.json` |\n| The judgement reasons onward once it has the facts | The custom-chip question's request of 7-14, sent 3 times in each of the three draws: as it was, 9/9 \"below $40 billion\"; with the Broadcom, Trainium and other facts written in that draw's ledger added, 9/9 left the lowest rung (6 times $40–60 billion, 3 times $60–80 billion), reasoning as the two readers did (\"guidance $16 billion, about $64 billion annualised, less networking chips\") | `predictions-one-test.md`, `one-test-result.json`, `log.md` row 8 |\n| Where the parking lot came from | D273: with the fallback sentence added, the core items on the extraction ruler went 64 → 68; the extraction ruler does not look at which question a fact is filed under (AGENTS §7.1, \"What it does not measure\") | `docs/DECISIONS.md` D273 |\n| What the parking lot holds | The figures above; an independent reader on 12 random articles: of 25 misfilings as it was, 21 were parked in the revenue question; 8 and 5 with the fallback deleted | `sink_by_standard.py`, the independent reader's report (`log.md` row 8) |\n\nAll files above are in `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/` unless noted otherwise.\n\n## 3. Ruled out or secondary (outside this phase's scope, each recorded separately)\n\n| Matter | Conclusion | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| The argument card | Not built; its code is deleted (Alex: \"好，删掉卡片代码\") | `docs/research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md` rows 4–11 |\n| The arrows of the question graph | Really wired backwards: a seed question's arrow means \"supports\" (D208), while the judging code reads it as \"whose conclusion to read\" (PRD 06). As a result themes are judged only after the total-revenue question, so the total-revenue question reads the themes' conclusions of the previous day, and in draw 3 a chain of questions went wrong in turn. But it does not explain the misfiling (filing comes before judging), and the gold itself judges data-center revenue as \"total revenue × 92%\". A topic of its own; settled by D368 (item 4: the arrow means \"supports\"), its fix to be built and measured | `core-problem.md`, `review-core-codex.md` |\n| Code removes the total-revenue question's own figures | True (\"keep only the narrowest question\" takes a seed arrow for \"a narrower sub-question\"), but each draw it costs the total-revenue question only 0–2 of the facts it needs | `log.md` row 8 |\n| A filing re-check added at the end | Recovers some, and misfiles about as many (independent reader: about one misfiled for each one filed right); not the solution | The independent reader's report |\n| One general sentence, \"the other party's figure in a deal counts too\" | The custom-chip question gains, but it pulls Morgan Stanley's price for a Rubin rack from the Rubin revenue question to the capital-spending question, and leaves some facts with no home | `answers.json` (the two arms definition and definition_no_fallback), `measure-corrected.txt` |\n| Tightening D259's \"leeway\" | Alex's own decision; this phase does not overturn it | D259 |\n| Opening questions (the Ohio guarantee was not opened); the two readers' disagreement on the China-share question | Another class of problem, not in this phase | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/diagnosis.md` §0 |\n| Model drift | With the same requests, today about half as many facts go into the total-revenue question as on 11-03; the cause is not proven. Compare only with a control re-sent the same day, never with the archive | `log.md` row 6 |\n\n## 4. Constraints (what must not move, and why)\n\n- **The frozen ruler** (AGENTS §7.1, D261, D262): the extraction standard, version 5 (the signed version 3 with D248's seven boundaries and D250's four\n  evidence boundaries and counting unit), golden-v5, the seed questions and the judgement gold; not a word changes; a disagreement is a gap in the\n  system (D263).\n- **The frozen extraction prompt** (D274): v74i (`poc-v108`) does not change by a word; what this phase changes is the one place that holds the filing\n  rule (the description of the `links` field), made into a new version with a new configuration and compared with v74i. Alex has given his word for this\n  work (2026-11-04: \"好你去解决问题\", \"开始做\"); making it the default needs his word again.\n- **Frozen opening and judging** (D354): this phase does not touch them.\n- **The standard's text** (in translation): §6, \"file under the narrowest open question; when no question takes it, record no home and drop it, and read\n  each one at evaluation\"; §5.1, \"makes the answer to some question more or less likely\", with four paths, \"demand, supply, competition, pricing\"; §5.3,\n  \"another company's matter is not kept when one cannot say which question about the covered company it moves through a path such as demand, supply,\n  competition or pricing\".\n- **Decisions**: D207 (one home per fact, the narrowest question), D209 (no home means dropped, each one read), D259 (leeway: a figure question takes\n  \"the demand, supply, competition and pricing that make it more or less likely\"; the total-revenue question taking more is an accepted cost, \"bounded by\n  the narrowest-question rule and the driver questions\"), D265 (code keeps only the narrowest), D273 (the fallback sentence), D355 (the two failed tests\n  of the previous filing topic).\n- **Prompt principles** (AGENTS §6): carry only the standard and add no new rule; a general hedge-fund analyst: every rule and example reads the same\n  for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip company, names neither NVIDIA nor its products or figures, and is not taken from a test article; a\n  classification is written as a closed set with two or three examples per class, replacing the abstract wording; quality is not fixed by lengthening\n  the prompt: remove as much as is added, or write down the reason.\n- **Code decides only \"is it the same thing\", never \"does it matter\"** (AGENTS §2).\n\n## 5. What to do\n\nStatus: the links-rule version that carried items 1–3 (v74l) failed its one test (§8 step 5); D361 keeps the fallback sentence, so item 3 is not carried out. The plan below is kept as written.\n\n1. **Replace the abstract sentence \"makes the answer more or less likely through demand, supply, competition or pricing\" with the few classes in which an analyst recognises an indirect relation, written as a closed set, each class with two or three examples from other industries** (AGENTS §6: one\n   abstract sentence is a coin flip on every send; examples replace it). A first draft of the classes (checked against the standard line by line at\n   design time; it holds only meanings the standard already has):\n   - The question's own figure: this question's figures, guidance, estimates and revisions (estimates for another period or another population follow\n     the existing rule).\n   - The other side of the same money: a seller's revenue from the buyers the question counts; those buyers' orders and backlog with these sellers.\n   - Price and volume: a product's price or shipments, for the question on that product's revenue.\n   - Variants and parts: a product's variants, alternatives, key parts and schedule changes, for the question on that product's launch.\n   - Demand, supply and competition moves with a number: customers' orders and capital-spending plans, suppliers' capacity and prices, competitors'\n     sales and share, for the question they affect.\n2. **State how to file a fact when two specific questions both bear on it** (the problem the `definition_no_fallback` arm exposed: Morgan Stanley's rack\n   price was filed under the buyers' capital-spending question, and the seller's Rubin revenue question lost it). One home per fact (D207): file it under\n   the question its figure measures most directly (for example, a hotel's room rate goes under its room-revenue question, not under the\n   travellers'-spending question; a parts maker's revenue from carmakers goes under the carmakers' parts-spending question, not under a rival parts\n   maker's share question); when one sentence gives a separate figure for each of two questions, write two items, each filed under its own question\n   (code stores two items that quote the same sentence as one record linked to both questions); never also file it under a broader question about the\n   same company (the failure of D355's test 2: the model filed it under an NVIDIA revenue question as well). The original draft's \"when the other\n   party's question is open … file it there as well\" conflicted with D207 and was deleted on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement (D360).\n3. **Delete the fallback sentence** and return to the standard's §6: when no question takes a fact, it is not filed; code drops it as \"no home\" and\n   records it (D209), and evaluation reads each one.\n4. Change only the one place that holds the filing rule; report its length in characters before and after, and write down the reason for any growth\n   (this time's reason: examples replace one abstract sentence).\n\n## 6. How to measure (the ruler does not move; the method does not change again)\n\n- **Requests**: rebuild each stored request byte for byte with the production code, changing only the one place that holds the filing rule; the\n  rebuilt request's archive id must equal the original's, or it is not sent (`resend_filing.py`, AGENTS §5). Never re-send the archive's copy whose\n  keys were sorted alphabetically.\n- **Articles**: development set = the 54 articles of `selection.json` (already read many times); held-out set = articles the extraction gold read and\n  the judgement gold uses that are not among those 54, drawn once before the test, with the list frozen and never changed afterwards. Both sets are\n  measured and reported apart.\n- **Control**: the unchanged requests re-sent 3 times the same day. No comparison with the archive (model drift).\n- **Each answer**: goes through the production code checks and filing first (including \"keep only the narrowest\" and \"no home means dropped\"), and is\n  counted after.\n- **What is counted** (`measure_filing.py`, with its matching rule fixed: items are matched on the distinct numbers and the proper nouns other than\n  NVIDIA in the source text; a source passage the system quotes that overlaps the gold's passage also counts as the same matter; \"optional\" counts as\n  optional; the citations in the body of the gold's answers are read):\n  - whether each fact that matters (one the gold uses to judge any question) reached the question that uses it, counted per fact, not per \"fact ×\n    question\";\n  - per question: the facts that matter that reached it and the new noise that appeared, counted by the decision rule below;\n  - the parking lot: how many facts the total-revenue question (v1, together with v22) takes in, and what they are;\n  - noise: how many of the sentences the standard does not keep are kept; per question, how noise is filed (links on facts the standard does not keep\n    or no question uses);\n  - how many core and supporting facts appear; the facts that matter that are dropped; how many questions each fact is filed under on average.\n  - Matching still has a small error (spot check: the new rule mismatches a few and misses a few); say so when reporting the numbers, and read the\n    ones that matter one by one.\n- **Decision rule** (rewritten on 2026-11-04 with Alex's agreement, D360. The original draft required \"every draw above the highest of the control's\n  three\" and the like, which the control itself fails when measured again, so it cannot tell good from bad. Script `decide.py`; written down and frozen\n  before each test; each draw's numbers and the totals are all reported):\n  - **Totals, with luck ruled out first**: each article's 6 answers from the new and the old arm are randomly reassigned between the two arms 4,000\n    times (with a fixed random seed); the new rule's difference counts as a real change only when fewer than 5% of the reassignments reach it.\n    - Development set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must rise; the count under the total-revenue questions (v1, v22) must\n      fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core facts must not fall.\n    - Held-out set: facts that matter reaching the question that uses them must not fall; sentences the standard does not keep must not rise; core\n      facts must not fall.\n  - **Per question, counted by code against the gold** (development and held-out sets together):\n    - A fact that matters which reaches the question at least two fewer times under the new rule than under the control counts as \"one fewer\" for that\n      question; in under the control all three times and under the new rule none of the three, it counts as \"lost outright\". A move to another question\n      that the gold also uses it for and that is no broader than the original (one home per fact, D207) does not count as fewer; a move to a broader\n      question counts. \"One more\" in the opposite direction offsets it.\n    - A noise sentence (not kept by the standard, or kept but used by no question) that the new rule files under the question at least twice while the\n      control never does counts as \"new noise\"; filed all three times, it counts as \"outright new noise\". The opposite direction offsets it.\n    - Any question with a net 3 fewer, a net 2 lost outright, a net 5 more new noise, or a net 3 more outright new noise fails. These thresholds are the\n      smallest values that keep \"misjudged when new and old are exactly the same\" within about one in ten; at the test, first compute the\n      misjudgement rate from the reassignments; if it is above one in ten, raise the threshold most prone to misjudgement by one step, then compare with\n      what was measured.\n  - **Smaller changes** (a question 2 fewer, two or three more noise) cannot be told from luck in three measurements: all are listed, given to a reader\n    who did not write the rule to read against the raw answers, and written into the report; they do not decide pass or fail.\n  Only when everything passes does it become a candidate; a candidate runs end to end three times on the 14-day window (extraction re-sent, matching and\n  judging run as usual, scored on the frozen judgement ruler), and that step needs Alex's word.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n### 7.1 The ruler\n\n- **One ruler.** Every gold, judge, prompt and acceptance uses the one standard named before the first arm. A second ruler in use (an old\n  reference, a judge's rubric, a prompt's own categories) is a defect, fixed before anything is measured (D241, Alex: \"我们今天一直浪费时间在不同标准之间来回\").\n- **The frozen ruler (D261, D262; 2026-11-02)** remains the standard for existing measurements and historical comparisons until a separately reviewed replacement is established. For future evidence scoring (D372), combine the existing gold's core and supporting as helpful, treat its not-kept entries as unhelpful, and leave optional entries neutral; this does not alter the frozen files. Its pieces, with the hashes code checks:\n  1. The extraction standard: `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, its version 5 (version 3 as signed in D243, with D248's seven\n     boundaries and D250's four evidence boundaries and counting unit); the gold `docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/golden-v5/` (dev sha256 `6f9476bb…`, test `af2145cd…`, recorded\n     in `golden-v5.sha256`). There is no version 6.\n  2. The questions: golden-v5's must_open / may_open (questions standard version 3) and the seeds `poc/seeds/nvda-2026-07-01-v2.json`\n     (`fca16f42…`, 22 questions). The seeds are part of the ruler: the judgement scorer refuses a run whose seed questions differ; a new\n     seed set is a new ruler version, opened only by Alex's decision.\n  3. The judgement ruler (D3): `docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/`: `ruler-v1.md` (the definition), `reader-brief.md`,\n     `packet-v1.json` (golden-v5's 309 items, `53d1e8b4…`), `questions-v1.json` (the 22 seeds plus the Ohio guarantee, `30854180…`),\n     `gold-v1.json` = reader B's answers (`636c056d…`, in `gold-v1.sha256`), `score_judgement.py` (refuses any other sha256 or ruler\n     version), `corrections-v1.json` (dated records only, printed with every score, never merged).\n\n  None of these files changes again (`tests/test_frozen_rulers.py` fails the suite when a hash moves; Alex, 2026-11-02: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，\n  已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重 … 我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\"). A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold,\n  with its reason and its before and after, printed with every score and never merged in. Every measurement names the gold version it used. A new piece (the D2\n  matter-to-question mapping, not yet built, is one) is an addition recorded as such, never an edit of these. A new version of any piece\n  exists only by Alex's decision, derives its gold from scratch, and old scores are never compared with it. A disagreement between the\n  system and the gold is a gap in the system to close (D263), never a case for the ruler. A suspected inconsistency between gold and\n  standard no longer stops an arm: record the concern separately, continue scoring on the unchanged frozen gold, and disclose it with the results (D373).\n  What it measures: extraction against the gold's items, questions against must_open / may_open, the judgement at the window end\n  2026-07-14 against reader B's ranges (a numeric question agrees when the gold range overlaps the chosen rung's band, a yes/no question\n  when the answers match). What it does not measure: the judgement's daily path, and whether evidence was filed under the right question.\n- **The extraction standard** (piece 1) is the extraction step's PRD, signed by Alex on 2026-10-29 (D243: \"其他几条的意见我都ok，sign off\"),\n  which replaced the first version (D229: \"按照这套标准来开始做测量，这条标准不要漂移\"). It holds the ledger's three records, the five question\n  types, the opening tests, the evidence rule and its reject list, source tiers, weight, and how a prompt change is written, measured and\n  iterated. No arm, gold, judge or prompt adds a rule, an example or a weight the page does not hold; a change is a recorded decision in\n  Alex's words first, then a new version of the page, then a drift review.\n- **A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again** (D261). Reviewed means readers who did not write it have read it\n  against the decisions and Alex has signed it. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored\n  against it before.\n- **The ruler is Alex's, never your own.** Gold, unit and the judge's reading are checked against what the product uses and fixed with\n  Alex before the first arm. A standard or reference you write gives every sentence its source (the signed standard, a decision, a PRD)\n  or lists it for Alex's decision with a lean; settling wording is no licence to change behaviour. After each rewrite, a read-only Codex\n  review against the decisions looks for unsourced rules, contradictions and misquotes, round after round until only wording-level\n  findings remain; clarity is tested apart, by independent readers on cases fixed before the text changes. A failed registered acceptance\n  stops the line and goes to Alex with its census; the next arm is never designed alone.\n- **Nobody grades their own change with a ruler still being corrected.** The reference is one Alex can read, reviewed and frozen before\n  the arms; a number scored against a ruler its author keeps correcting is not a conclusion. Meaning is judged by a reader who did not\n  write the change; code checks only structure and counts (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"我根本无法相信你的评价\").\n- **A new gold** (only for a new ruler version Alex opens). The unit is fixed before the first send (for extraction, one research matter\n  in one article, which several records may express; signed standard §11) and the gold is written from the complete material the model\n  sees before any answer is read. Each item holds the exact source span (checked by code), the standard line it follows, its weight under the signed rule and, where\n  proposals are pending, its weight under them with the proposals it depends on named.\n  A blind second reader reads the same sources; every disagreement is decided against the source and its reason recorded. The gold is\n  frozen with its sha256 and never edited after a send. Model-authored gold and model judges are labelled as such. A held-out set no arm\n  has seen is in from the first arm.\n- **Measure the stick before using it:** control against a second control, the criterion's null estimated (a conjunction over many items\n  fails by chance), and its workload sized from its rules. Tune on dev; score test once per configuration.\n## D711 · 2026-11-21 · Pilot pair 1 is inconclusive (control double refusal); the comparison is closed; council round 37 recommends a citation-only judge version to Alex\n\n- **Alex's words** (2026-11-21, on the stopped control): \"好你跑一次council 看trace 同意了就开始下一步\".\n- **Registered verdict:** inconclusive. control-1 (poc-v118) stopped on 09-08 when v21's answer and its retry each cited an id outside\n  the listed evidence (`e362` for `e3620`; `e3111` beside `e3110`/`e3112`), PAID-DESIGN.md §4 (2). linked-1 completed with every\n  acceptance check true. control-1 equals old-2 on every H2 table through 09-07. Spend $1.70 of $2.50.\n- **Exploratory, one pair, one draw, beside the verdict** (`whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md`):\n  - P: the parser counts 3 of 60 dates (linked-1) against 28 of 60 (control-1) on 07-10..09-07. All 12 flagged linked dates were read:\n    none has Data Center above total revenue (parser artefacts). The 5 sampled control dates are real.\n  - H4: four linked v14 answers (07-15..07-18) add v8's stand-alone CPU forecast to a total built from company guidance, read by Claude\n    and, shuffled, by Codex.\n  - H1: 5 linked against 1 control refusal on the 200 matched reader-days, at the harm line.\n  - Every refused judge answer seen is an id-membership error: 17 in 5,408 distinct attempts. 6 of linked-1's 7 fresh reader refusals\n    put an id in the wrong list, though the request's closing instruction forbids it.\n- **Council round 37** (`round37-brief.md`, `codex-r37.md`, `claude-r37.md`, `round37b-brief.md`, `codex-r37b.md`), consensus A:\n  - pair 1 is closed, with no redraw (B) and no resume (C);\n  - C would move H1 across its line through the refusals that invalidated the control, and its rule was proposed after the stop was\n    seen;\n  - Claude proposed C first and withdrew it on linked-1's H1 numbers;\n  - a resume-once rule may be registered only for a future comparison, before its send, in both arms, and proven on stored data.\n- **Recommendation to Alex (his to open, a new version of the frozen judge):**\n  - The version: a judge version that changes the citation format only. Every id field (cites, push ids, `cites_views`, theme\n    pushes) takes a closed list built from the exact request.\n  - The test, at $0, end to end: stored accepted answers fit; observed bad ids are excluded; an empty list is the only answer for a\n    field with no allowed id.\n  - A separate design, not part of this version: the link direction (a whole reading its own part). The keys label stand-alone CPU\n    `other`, and the direction is a judgement, which D704 left open on purpose.\n- **Not done:** no paid call after the pilot, no product file changed.\n\n## D712 · 2026-11-21 · Alex opens a citation-only judge version (closed per-request id lists), tested at $0 first\n\n- **The question:** \"试点到此收尾（结论\"说不准\"，花了 1.70 美元）。发现了两个问题：一是模型常写出不在名单上的编号，回答因此被退回，这次对照组就是因为这个停下；二是新版本让\"总收入\"把 CPU 收入又加了一遍。下一步做哪个？\"\n  Options: 开引用格式新版本 (recommended: every id field of the judge's answer takes a closed list built from the request; $0 check on\n  stored data that accepted answers still pass and the bad ids are excluded; asking again before any paid test); 先设计重复计算的修法;\n  先停在这里.\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-21): \"开引用格式新版本 (推荐)\".\n- **Scope:** a new judge version whose only change is the answer format's id fields (D711's recommendation). The link direction stays\n  a separate design. Design, then council review, then build with tests and mutants, then the $0 test; any paid test asks Alex again.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '55,95p;120,265p;296,360p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py | sed -n '34,111p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py | sed -n '29,82p'; nl -ba scripts/replay.py | sed -n '72,116p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '55,95p;120,265p;296,360p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py | sed -n '34,111p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/rebuild_control.py | sed -n '29,82p'; nl -ba scripts/replay.py | sed -n '72,116p'\"","aggregated_output":"    55\tdef schema_for(prompt_version):\n    56\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n    57\t    pushes = PUSHES\n    58\t    schema = {\n    59\t        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n    60\t        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\n    61\t        'properties': {\n    62\t            'rung': {'type': 'integer'}, 'reasons': {'type': 'string'},\n    63\t            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\n    64\t            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\n    65\t                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n    66\t            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\n    67\t        },\n    68\t    }\n    69\t    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n    70\t    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n    71\t                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n    72\t    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\n    73\t    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\n    74\t    return schema\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\n    78\t    \"\"\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\n    79\t    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\"\"\"\n    80\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n    81\t        return []\n    82\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n    83\t    out = []\n    84\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select view_id from views where object_kind='theme' order by view_id\"):\n    85\t        theme_id = row['view_id']\n    86\t        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\n    87\t        if not state or not store.is_open(conn, theme_id):\n    88\t            continue\n    89\t        updated = bool(last) and bool(conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and changed=1 and judgement_id>? limit 1',\n    90\t                                                   (theme_id, last['judgement_id'])).fetchone())\n    91\t        rung = store.rungs_of(conn, theme_id)[state['rung'] - 1]\n    92\t        out.append({'view_id': theme_id, 'view': store.view(conn, theme_id), 'state': state, 'rung_label': rung['label'], 'updated': updated})\n    93\t    return out\n    94\t\n    95\t\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\tdef _indented(text, indent='        '):\n   123\t    \"\"\"A stored value inside a block: every continuation line indented, so no physical line can read as a header or a listed id.\"\"\"\n   124\t    return str(text).replace('\\r\\n', '\\n').replace('\\n', '\\n' + indent)\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\tdef _dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag):\n   128\t    \"\"\"judging-v8 (D694, design §3): the read judgement's comparison point and the system's forecast in full, labelled as ours, beside\n   129\t    the reasons excerpt; the read question not judged yet shows only that.\"\"\"\n   130\t    if not state:\n   131\t        return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now not judged yet']\n   132\t    return [f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {rung_label}, judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}',\n   133\t            f'    Comparison point stated by that judgement: {_indented(state.get(\"reference\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   134\t            f'    The system\\'s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): {_indented(state.get(\"implied_outcome\") or \"not stated\")}',\n   135\t            f'    Reasons (excerpt): {_indented((state.get(\"reasons\") or \"\")[:600])}']\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0, full_dependencies=False):\n   139\t    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown. full_dependencies: the judging-v8 dependency block.\"\"\"\n   140\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n   141\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n   142\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n   143\t    if hidden:\n   144\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n   145\t    for p in pieces:\n   146\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   147\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   148\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   149\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   150\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   151\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   152\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   153\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   154\t    if deps:\n   155\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   156\t        for d in deps:\n   157\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   158\t            if not target:\n   159\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   160\t                continue\n   161\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   162\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   163\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   164\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   165\t            if full_dependencies:\n   166\t                lines.extend(_dependency_lines_full(conn, target, d, state, rung_label, tv, flag))\n   167\t                continue\n   168\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   169\t    if themes:\n   170\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   171\t        for theme in themes:\n   172\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   173\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   174\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   175\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   176\t    if last:\n   177\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   178\t    else:\n   179\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   180\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   181\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   182\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   183\t    return lines\n   184\t\n   185\t\n   186\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   187\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   188\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   189\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   190\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n   191\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n   192\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   193\t    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes_in_force(conn, view_id), hidden=hidden,\n   194\t                           full_dependencies=prompt_version in FULL_DEPENDENCY_BLOCK)\n   195\t    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   196\t        return handle.read(), '\\n'.join(lines)\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\tdef retry_note(errors):\n   200\t    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n   201\t\n   202\t\n   203\tdef themes_shown_in(request_text):\n   204\t    \"\"\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\"\"\"\n   205\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\n   206\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\tdef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n   210\t    \"\"\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\"\"\"\n   211\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n   212\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   213\t\n   214\t\n   215\tdef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None):\n   216\t    \"\"\"request_text: the user message that was sent, so theme and evidence ids are checked against what it carried (a theme may have\n   217\t    closed or opened since); without it, against what the ledger would show now.\"\"\"\n   218\t    errors = []\n   219\t    shown = themes_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {theme['view_id'] for theme in themes_in_force(conn, view_id)}\n   220\t    named = []\n   221\t    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n   222\t        if entry['view_id'] in named:\n   223\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n   224\t        elif entry['view_id'] not in shown:\n   225\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is not a theme in force shown to {view_id}')\n   226\t        named.append(entry['view_id'])\n   227\t    # the closed set is what the request showed (D198), read from the text that was sent, else computed from the ledger\n   228\t    allowed = evidence_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {p['evidence_id'] for p in evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)[0]}\n   229\t    not_allowed = lambda e: f'{e} is not among the evidence shown to {view_id}'\n   230\t    bad_push = lambda e: f'push on {e} which was not shown to {view_id}'\n   231\t    deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n   232\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   233\t    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):\n   234\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\n   235\t    for cited in data['cites']:\n   236\t        if cited not in allowed:\n   237\t            errors.append(not_allowed(cited))\n   238\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n   239\t        if cited not in deps:\n   240\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\n   241\t    for push in data['pushes']:\n   242\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\n   243\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\n   244\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\n   245\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n   246\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n   247\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   248\t    if last is None and not data['changed']:\n   249\t        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\n   250\t    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\n   251\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\"rung\"]} to {data[\"rung\"]} but changed is false')\n   252\t    return errors\n   253\t\n   254\t\n   255\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\n   256\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\n   257\t    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\n   258\t                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),\n   259\t                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,\n   260\t                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\n   261\t                                reference=data.get('reference'), implied_outcome=data.get('implied_outcome'),\n   262\t                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,\n   263\t                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])\n   264\t    conn.commit()\n   265\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}\n   296\tdef queued_by_ledger(conn, seq):\n   297\t    \"\"\"What the judgements already committed at this sequence number queued; a fresh round finds nothing here, a resumed round\n   298\t    finds what the interrupted one had queued in memory.\"\"\"\n   299\t    queued = []\n   300\t    for row in conn.execute('select view_id from judgements where seq=? and changed=1 order by judgement_id', (seq,)):\n   301\t        queued.extend(queued_by_change(conn, row['view_id']))\n   302\t    return queued\n   303\t\n   304\t\n   305\tdef round_of_judgements(archive, cfg, conn, changed_views, seq, item, *, transport=None):\n   306\t    \"\"\"Judge the open views in changed_views, dependencies first; a changed conclusion queues open dependants.\n   307\t\n   308\t    Views that do not depend on each other are judged at the same time: each level of the dependency order is sent\n   309\t    to the model concurrently (the prompts are built and the answers checked and written in this thread, so the\n   310\t    database connection never crosses threads). A view waits while anything upstream of it is still pending, so a\n   311\t    dependant always reads this round's conclusion of its dependency. A view with no evidence in force stays\n   312\t    unjudged (D59), and a view already judged at this sequence number (a resumed round) is not judged twice.\n   313\t\n   314\t    Among the views ready to be judged, theme theses go first, so an asset thesis reads this round's theme conclusions; a theme judgement that says changed queues every open asset thesis with\n   315\t    evidence in force. The starting queue adds what the ledger says earlier commits at this sequence number queued.\"\"\"\n   316\t    import concurrent.futures\n   317\t\n   318\t    version = cfg.rejudging.prompt_version\n   319\t    schema = schema_for(version)\n   320\t\n   321\t    def eligible(view_id):\n   322\t        return store.is_open(conn, view_id) and not store.has_judgement(conn, view_id, seq) and bool(store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id))\n   323\t\n   324\t    def is_theme(view_id):\n   325\t        return store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme'\n   326\t\n   327\t    pending = [v for v in topological(conn, list(changed_views) + queued_by_ledger(conn, seq)) if eligible(v)]\n   328\t    done, results = set(), []\n   329\t    while pending:\n   330\t        ready = [v for v in pending if upstream(conn, v).isdisjoint(set(pending) - {v})] or pending[:1]\n   331\t        level = [v for v in ready if is_theme(v)] or ready\n   332\t        prompts = {v: build_prompt(conn, v, version) for v in level}\n   333\t\n   334\t        def ask(view_id, note=''):\n   335\t            system, user = prompts[view_id]\n   336\t            return model.call(archive, cfg, cfg.rejudging, system, user + note, schema, 'judgement', 'judge', transport=transport)\n   337\t\n   338\t        with concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=JUDGE_WORKERS) as pool_:\n   339\t            answers = dict(zip(level, pool_.map(ask, level)))\n   340\t        for view_id in level:\n   341\t            answer = answers[view_id]\n   342\t            errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   343\t            if errors:\n   344\t                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\n   345\t                answer = ask(view_id, retry_note(errors))\n   346\t                errors = check_answer(conn, view_id, answer.data, prompts[view_id][1])\n   347\t                if errors:\n   348\t                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\n   349\t                    raise JudgementRefused(f'{view_id}: ' + '; '.join(errors))\n   350\t            result = _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer)\n   351\t            done.add(view_id)\n   352\t            results.append(result)\n   353\t            if result['changed']:\n   354\t                for dependant in queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   355\t                    if dependant not in done and dependant not in pending and eligible(dependant):\n   356\t                        pending.append(dependant)\n   357\t        pending = [v for v in topological(conn, pending) if v not in done and eligible(v)]\n   358\t    return results\n    34\t\n    35\tOLD2 = july_test.OLD2\n    36\tITEMS = july_test.ITEMS\n    37\tV119 = july_test.V119\n    38\tUNIVERSE = july_test.UNIVERSE\n    39\tWINDOW = ('2026-07-01', '2026-09-20')\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef refused_rows():\n    43\t    \"\"\"old-2's answers its own run refused (the archive keeps them under the request's hash with a ':refused:' suffix, so no later\n    44\t    identical request is answered with them): {request hash: stored provider response}. A replay must meet each refusal again to\n    45\t    reach the stored retry.\"\"\"\n    46\t    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"archive.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    47\t    return {sha.split(':refused:')[0]: json.loads(response) for sha, response in\n    48\t            stored.execute(\"select request_sha256, response_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:refused:%' order by call_id\")}\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef replay_window(folder, link_answer, cfg_path=V119):\n    52\t    \"\"\"poc-v119 from an empty ledger over the whole window: link questions go to `link_answer`; every other request must be answered\n    53\t    from the copy of old-2's archive (an answer old-2's own run refused is given back once, so the check refuses it again); anything\n    54\t    else stops the pass. Returns the census: equality with old-2, every link job, every opening with its pairs.\"\"\"\n    55\t    if folder.exists():\n    56\t        raise SystemExit(f'{folder} exists: a pass starts from an empty folder')\n    57\t    folder.mkdir(parents=True)\n    58\t    shutil.copyfile(OLD2 / 'archive.sqlite', folder / 'archive.sqlite')\n    59\t    views = folder / 'views.sqlite'\n    60\t    marker = sqlite3.connect(views)                 # marked harness-only before the first item: ordinary writers refuse it (D694 §0)\n    61\t    marker.execute('create table harness_only (name text, day text)')\n    62\t    marker.execute(\"insert into harness_only values ('window_test.py', '2026-11-21')\")\n    63\t    marker.commit()\n    64\t    marker.close()\n    65\t    held = live_lock.acquire(str(views))            # the store lock for the whole pass: no second writer\n    66\t    asked, refused_again = [], []\n    67\t    stored_refusals = refused_rows()\n    68\t\n    69\t    def transport(*args):\n    70\t        if len(args) == 1 and july_test.is_link_request(args[0]):\n    71\t            asked.append(sorted(args[0]['questions']))\n    72\t            return link_answer(args[0])\n    73\t        response = stored_refusals.pop(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1], None)\n    74\t        if response is not None:                   # old-2's own run refused this answer: give it back, so the check refuses it again\n    75\t            refused_again.append(model.request_identity(args[-1])[1][:12])\n    76\t            return response\n    77\t        (folder / 'missed-request.json').write_text(json.dumps(args[-1], ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\n    78\t        raise july_test.Stop('a request other than a link question missed the archive')\n    79\t    started = time.time()\n    80\t    try:\n    81\t        totals = replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(views), archive=model.Archive(str(folder / 'archive.sqlite')),\n    82\t                            cfg=config.load(str(cfg_path)), universe=universe.load(str(UNIVERSE)), from_day=WINDOW[0], until_day=WINDOW[1],\n    83\t                            transport=transport, log=lambda *a: None, only_objects={'NVDA'})\n    84\t    finally:\n    85\t        live_lock.release(held)\n    86\t    print('totals:', totals, 'seconds:', round(time.time() - started))\n    87\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{folder / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    88\t    last_seq = conn.execute('select max(seq) from days_completed').fetchone()[0]\n    89\t    stored_last = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2 / \"views.sqlite\"}?mode=ro', uri=True).execute('select max(seq) from days_completed').fetchone()[0]\n    90\t    print('last completed seq', last_seq, 'old-2', stored_last)\n    91\t    equal = last_seq == stored_last and rebuild_control.compare(folder / 'views.sqlite', last_seq)\n    92\t    openings = []\n    93\t    for attempt, seq, status, record_json in conn.execute('select attempt_id, seq, status, record_json from link_selections order by id'):\n    94\t        record = json.loads(record_json)\n    95\t        if status == 'proposed' and record.get('pairs'):\n    96\t            openings.append({'attempt': attempt, 'seq': seq, 'pairs': record['pairs'], 'calls': record.get('calls', []),\n    97\t                             'proposed': record.get('proposed', []), 'corrections': record.get('corrections', [])})\n    98\t    census = {'equal to old-2': equal, 'link jobs asked': len(asked), 'questions in them': sum(len(a) for a in asked),\n    99\t              \"old-2's refused answers met again\": refused_again, 'left unmet': sorted(sha[:12] for sha in stored_refusals),\n   100\t              'link rows written': conn.execute(\"select count(*) from dependencies where kind='reads'\").fetchone()[0],\n   101\t              'openings with a pair shown': openings}\n   102\t    (folder / 'census.json').write_text(json.dumps(census, indent=1))\n   103\t    print(json.dumps({k: v for k, v in census.items() if k != 'openings with a pair shown'}, indent=1))\n   104\t    for opening in openings:\n   105\t        eligible = [p['thesis'] for p in opening['pairs'] if p.get('eligible')]\n   106\t        print(opening['seq'], 'eligible', eligible, 'not eligible', len(opening['pairs']) - len(eligible))\n   107\t    return census\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\tdef neither(scratch):\n   111\t    return replay_window(scratch / 'neither-v119', july_test.fake_jev(set()))['equal to old-2']\n    29\tdef refuse(*args, **kwargs):\n    30\t    raise SendRefused('a request was not in the archive: the rebuilt request differs from the stored one')\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\tdef rows(conn, sql, args=()):\n    34\t    return [tuple(r) for r in conn.execute(sql, args)]\n    35\t\n    36\t\n    37\tdef compare(rebuilt_path, last_seq):\n    38\t    rebuilt = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{rebuilt_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    39\t    stored = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{OLD2}/views.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    40\t    checks = {\n    41\t        'views': ('select view_id, question, created_seq from views where created_seq <= ? order by view_id', (last_seq,)),\n    42\t        'view_keys': ('select view_id, measure, scope, period_start, period_end, unit from view_keys where seq <= ? order by view_id', (last_seq,)),\n    43\t        'evidence': ('select evidence_id, quote, created_seq from evidence where created_seq <= ? order by evidence_id', (last_seq,)),\n    44\t        'evidence_links': ('select evidence_id, view_id, seq from evidence_links where seq <= ? order by evidence_id, view_id', (last_seq,)),\n    45\t        'judgements': ('select view_id, seq, rung, reasons, cited_evidence_json, cited_views_json, changed, reference, implied_outcome, request_sha256 from judgements where seq <= ? order by judgement_id', (last_seq,)),\n    46\t        'rungs': ('select r.view_id, r.position, r.label, r.condition, r.lo, r.hi from rungs r join views v using(view_id) where v.created_seq <= ? order by r.view_id, r.position', (last_seq,)),\n    47\t        'view_switches': ('select view_id, open, reason, after_seq from view_switches where after_seq <= ? order by id', (last_seq,)),\n    48\t        'successions': ('select view_id, succeeds, seq from successions where seq <= ? order by id', (last_seq,)),\n    49\t        'dependencies': ('select view_id, depends_on, seq from dependencies where seq <= ? order by dependency_id', (last_seq,)),\n    50\t    }\n    51\t    ok = True\n    52\t    for name, (sql, args) in checks.items():\n    53\t        a, b = rows(rebuilt, sql, args), rows(stored, sql, args)\n    54\t        same = a == b\n    55\t        ok = ok and same\n    56\t        print(f'{name}: rebuilt {len(a)} stored {len(b)} {\"equal\" if same else \"DIFFER\"}')\n    57\t        if not same:\n    58\t            for x, y in zip(a, b):\n    59\t                if x != y:\n    60\t                    print('  first difference:', str(x)[:200], '|', str(y)[:200])\n    61\t                    break\n    62\t    return ok\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tdef main():\n    66\t    scratch = Path(sys.argv[1])\n    67\t    scratch.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    68\t    views_path, archive_path = scratch / 'views.sqlite', scratch / 'archive.sqlite'\n    69\t    for path in (views_path, archive_path):\n    70\t        if path.exists():\n    71\t            raise SystemExit(f'{path} exists: a rebuild starts from an empty folder')\n    72\t    shutil.copyfile(OLD2 / 'archive.sqlite', archive_path)\n    73\t    cfg = config.load(str(REPO / 'poc/config/poc-v118.json'))\n    74\t    uni = universe.load(str(REPO / 'poc/universe.json'))\n    75\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=str(ITEMS), views_path=str(views_path), archive=model.Archive(str(archive_path)), cfg=cfg,\n    76\t                        universe=uni, from_day='2026-07-01', until_day=UNTIL, transport=refuse, log=print,\n    77\t                        only_objects={'NVDA'})          # the comparison launcher's default (`budget_replay.py --only NVDA`)\n    78\t    print('totals:', totals)\n    79\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{views_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    80\t    last_seq = conn.execute('select max(seq) from days_completed where day=?', (UNTIL,)).fetchone()[0]\n    81\t    print('last completed seq at', UNTIL, last_seq)\n    82\t    sys.exit(0 if compare(views_path, last_seq) else 1)\n    72\tdef main():\n    73\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    74\t    parser.add_argument('--from', dest='from_day', required=True)\n    75\t    parser.add_argument('--until', dest='until_day', required=True)\n    76\t    parser.add_argument('--day0', default=None)\n    77\t    parser.add_argument('--testdb', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n    78\t    parser.add_argument('--views', required=True, help='the ledger this run writes (a new run: a new dated folder)')\n    79\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', required=True, help='the model-call archive of this run')\n    80\t    parser.add_argument('--config', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'config', 'poc-v118.json'))\n    81\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n    82\t    parser.add_argument('--only', default=None, help='comma-separated object ids to restrict the stream to')\n    83\t    parser.add_argument('--cap', type=float, default=None, help='USD spend cap for this run')\n    84\t    parser.add_argument('--max-items-per-day', type=int, default=None)\n    85\t    parser.add_argument('--workers', type=int, default=16, help='extraction requests prepared at a time (D183); 1 is the serial path')\n    86\t    parser.add_argument('--jev-workers', type=int, default=None,\n    87\t                        help='Jev matching questions sent at a time when --workers > 1; default 8 for Jev, 1 for another engine')\n    88\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n    89\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.views), exist_ok=True)\n    90\t    log_path = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(args.views), 'replay.log')\n    91\t\n    92\t    def log(*parts):\n    93\t        line = ' '.join(str(p) for p in parts)\n    94\t        print(line, flush=True)\n    95\t        with open(log_path, 'a', encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n    96\t            handle.write(line + '\\n')\n    97\t\n    98\t    cfg = config.load(args.config)\n    99\t    if cfg.baseline is not None:\n   100\t        raise SystemExit(f'config {cfg.version} uses retired seeded-question baseline; select a configuration without it')\n   101\t    refuse_links_engine(cfg)\n   102\t    refuse_seeded_ledger(args.views)\n   103\t    refuse_harness_ledger(args.views)\n   104\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n   105\t    archive = model.Archive(args.archive)\n   106\t    day_runner = None\n   107\t    if args.workers > 1:\n   108\t        jev_workers = args.jev_workers if args.jev_workers is not None else (8 if cfg.matching.engine == 'jev' else 1)\n   109\t        day_runner = parallel_day.ParallelDay(os.path.abspath(args.testdb), os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.views)), 'manifests'),\n   110\t                                              extraction_workers=args.workers, jev_workers=jev_workers)\n   111\t    log(f'--- replay {args.from_day}..{args.until_day} config {cfg.version}/{cfg.checksum} provider {cfg.provider} universe {uni.version}'\n   112\t        f' workers {args.workers}')\n   113\t    totals = replay.run(testdb_path=args.testdb, views_path=args.views, archive=archive, cfg=cfg, universe=uni,\n   114\t                        from_day=args.from_day, until_day=args.until_day, day0=args.day0, spend_cap_usd=args.cap, log=log,\n   115\t                        only_objects=set(args.only.split(',')) if args.only else None, max_items_per_day=args.max_items_per_day,\n   116\t                        day_runner=day_runner)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '69,286p'; nl -ba scripts/preflight.py | sed -n '1,106p;276,355p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '60,122p'; rg -n 'request_sha256.*(:refused:|:schema:|:malformed:)|archive\\\\.retire\\\\(' src scripts --glob '*.py'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '69,286p'; nl -ba scripts/preflight.py | sed -n '1,106p;276,355p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/jev.py | sed -n '60,122p'; rg -n 'request_sha256.*(:refused:|:schema:|:malformed:)|archive\\\\.retire\\\\(' src scripts --glob '*.py'\"","aggregated_output":"    69\tclass Archive:\n    70\t    \"\"\"Shared by the extraction worker threads: one connection, every access under a lock.\"\"\"\n    71\t\n    72\t    def __init__(self, path):\n    73\t        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)\n    74\t        self.conn = sqlite3.connect(path, check_same_thread=False)\n    75\t        self.conn.executescript(SCHEMA_SQL)\n    76\t        import threading\n    77\t        self.lock = threading.Lock()\n    78\t\n    79\t    def lookup(self, sha):\n    80\t        with self.lock:\n    81\t            return self.conn.execute('select call_id, answer_json, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (sha,)).fetchone()\n    82\t\n    83\t    def record(self, **fields):\n    84\t        \"\"\"One row per distinct request; a second identical request recorded at the same moment (two threads, or a\n    85\t        failed answer repeated within the same second) keeps the first row's id instead of failing.\"\"\"\n    86\t        columns = list(fields)\n    87\t        with self.lock:\n    88\t            cursor = self.conn.execute(f'insert or ignore into model_calls ({\",\".join(columns)}) values ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(columns))})',\n    89\t                                       [fields[c] for c in columns])\n    90\t            self.conn.commit()\n    91\t            if cursor.rowcount == 0:\n    92\t                return self.conn.execute('select call_id from model_calls where request_sha256=?', (fields['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()[0]\n    93\t            return cursor.lastrowid\n    94\t\n    95\t    def retire(self, call_id):\n    96\t        \"\"\"A code check refused this answer: the row stays for the record, but no later identical request is answered with it\n    97\t        (the same shape as a schema-refused or malformed row, whose hash carries a suffix).\"\"\"\n    98\t        with self.lock:\n    99\t            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\n   100\t                              (uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], call_id))\n   101\t            self.conn.commit()\n   102\t\n   103\t    def totals(self):\n   104\t        with self.lock:\n   105\t            return self.conn.execute('select count(*), coalesce(sum(cost_usd),0), coalesce(sum(input_tokens),0), coalesce(sum(output_tokens),0) from model_calls').fetchone()\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef _key(provider):\n   109\t    name = ENDPOINTS[provider][1]\n   110\t    if os.environ.get(name):\n   111\t        return os.environ[name]\n   112\t    with open(CREDENTIALS, encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   113\t        return json.load(handle)[name]\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tdef build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider):\n   117\t    request = {\n   118\t        'model': setting.model,\n   119\t        'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': system}, {'role': 'user', 'content': user}],\n   120\t        'response_format': {'type': 'json_schema', 'json_schema': {'name': schema_name, 'strict': True, 'schema': schema}},\n   121\t    }\n   122\t    if provider == 'openai':\n   123\t        request['max_completion_tokens'] = setting.max_output_tokens\n   124\t        if setting.reasoning_effort:\n   125\t            request['reasoning_effort'] = setting.reasoning_effort\n   126\t    else:\n   127\t        request['max_tokens'] = setting.max_output_tokens\n   128\t    return request\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\tdef openai_transport(provider, request, timeout=180, max_attempts=3):   # the default preserves the production retry behavior\n   132\t    url, _ = ENDPOINTS[provider]\n   133\t    body = json.dumps(request).encode('utf-8')\n   134\t    headers = {'Authorization': f'Bearer {_key(provider)}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'}\n   135\t    last = None\n   136\t    last_http = None\n   137\t    if isinstance(max_attempts, bool) or not isinstance(max_attempts, int) or max_attempts < 1:\n   138\t        raise ValueError('max_attempts must be a positive integer')\n   139\t    for attempt in range(max_attempts):\n   140\t        try:\n   141\t            with urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=headers, method='POST'), timeout=timeout) as response:\n   142\t                raw_bytes = response.read()\n   143\t                try:\n   144\t                    raw = raw_bytes.decode('utf-8')\n   145\t                except UnicodeDecodeError:\n   146\t                    if max_attempts != 1:\n   147\t                        raise\n   148\t                    failure = TransportError('invalid UTF-8 HTTP response')\n   149\t                    failure.response_body = raw_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace')\n   150\t                    failure.response_body_base64 = base64.b64encode(raw_bytes).decode('ascii')\n   151\t                    failure.http_status = response.status\n   152\t                    raise failure\n   153\t                try:\n   154\t                    return json.loads(raw)\n   155\t                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n   156\t                    if max_attempts != 1:\n   157\t                        raise\n   158\t                    failure = TransportError('malformed HTTP response')\n   159\t                    failure.response_body = raw\n   160\t                    failure.http_status = response.status\n   161\t                    raise failure\n   162\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:\n   163\t            body_bytes = error.read()\n   164\t            body_text = body_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace' if max_attempts == 1 else 'ignore')\n   165\t            last_http = (error.code, body_text, base64.b64encode(body_bytes).decode('ascii'))\n   166\t            last = f'HTTP {error.code}: {body_text[:600]}'\n   167\t            if error.code in (400, 401, 403, 404):\n   168\t                failure = TransportError(last)\n   169\t                failure.response_body = body_text\n   170\t                failure.response_body_base64 = last_http[2]\n   171\t                failure.http_status = error.code\n   172\t                raise failure\n   173\t        except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, ConnectionError, OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as error:   # a dropped or truncated response is retried like a network error\n   174\t            last = repr(error)[:200]\n   175\t            last_http = None   # the final failure describes the last attempt only\n   176\t        if max_attempts == 3 or attempt + 1 < max_attempts:\n   177\t            time.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   178\t    failure = TransportError(last or 'no answer')\n   179\t    if last_http:\n   180\t        failure.http_status, failure.response_body, failure.response_body_base64 = last_http\n   181\t    raise failure\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\tdef check_schema(value, schema, path='$', root=None):\n   185\t    \"\"\"A small validator for the subset of JSON Schema the prompts use: object/required/additionalProperties,\n   186\t    array/items/minItems, string/enum/pattern, integer, number, boolean, null in anyOf, and $ref into the root's $defs.\"\"\"\n   187\t    root = root if root is not None else schema\n   188\t    if '$ref' in schema:\n   189\t        name = schema['$ref'].rsplit('/', 1)[1]\n   190\t        schema = root['$defs'][name]\n   191\t    kind = schema.get('type')\n   192\t    if 'anyOf' in schema:\n   193\t        # a value matching no option reports the closest options' errors (fewest), not merely the last option's\n   194\t        failures = []\n   195\t        for option in schema['anyOf']:\n   196\t            errors = check_schema(value, option, path, root)\n   197\t            if not errors:\n   198\t                return []\n   199\t            failures.append(errors)\n   200\t        fewest = min((len(errors) for errors in failures), default=0)\n   201\t        closest = list(dict.fromkeys(error for errors in failures if len(errors) == fewest for error in errors))\n   202\t        return closest or [f'{path}: matches no option']\n   203\t    if kind == 'object':\n   204\t        if not isinstance(value, dict):\n   205\t            return [f'{path}: expected object']\n   206\t        errors = []\n   207\t        for name in schema.get('required', []):\n   208\t            if name not in value:\n   209\t                errors.append(f'{path}.{name}: required')\n   210\t        properties = schema.get('properties', {})\n   211\t        for name, item in value.items():\n   212\t            if name in properties:\n   213\t                errors.extend(check_schema(item, properties[name], f'{path}.{name}', root))\n   214\t            elif schema.get('additionalProperties') is False:\n   215\t                errors.append(f'{path}.{name}: not allowed')\n   216\t        return errors\n   217\t    if kind == 'array':\n   218\t        if not isinstance(value, list):\n   219\t            return [f'{path}: expected array']\n   220\t        errors = []\n   221\t        if len(value) < schema.get('minItems', 0):\n   222\t            errors.append(f'{path}: fewer than {schema[\"minItems\"]} items')\n   223\t        for index, item in enumerate(value):\n   224\t            errors.extend(check_schema(item, schema.get('items', {}), f'{path}[{index}]', root))\n   225\t        return errors\n   226\t    if kind == 'string':\n   227\t        if not isinstance(value, str):\n   228\t            return [f'{path}: expected string']\n   229\t        if 'enum' in schema and value not in schema['enum']:\n   230\t            return [f'{path}: {value!r} not in {schema[\"enum\"]}']\n   231\t        if 'pattern' in schema and not re.search(schema['pattern'], value):\n   232\t            return [f'{path}: {value!r} does not match {schema[\"pattern\"]}']\n   233\t        return []\n   234\t    if kind == 'integer':\n   235\t        return [] if isinstance(value, int) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected integer']\n   236\t    if kind == 'number':\n   237\t        return [] if isinstance(value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected number']\n   238\t    if kind == 'boolean':\n   239\t        return [] if isinstance(value, bool) else [f'{path}: expected boolean']\n   240\t    if kind == 'null':\n   241\t        return [] if value is None else [f'{path}: expected null']\n   242\t    return []\n   243\t\n   244\t\n   245\tdef request_identity(request):\n   246\t    \"\"\"The exact serialized request and its archive key, shared by callers and validation.\"\"\"\n   247\t    encoded = json.dumps(request, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)\n   248\t    return encoded, hashlib.sha256(encoded.encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   252\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   253\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   254\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   255\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   256\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   257\t    if hit:\n   258\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   259\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   260\t    started = time.time()\n   261\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   262\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n   263\t    try:\n   264\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   265\t        data = json.loads(content)\n   266\t    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n   267\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   268\t                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   269\t                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n   270\t                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   271\t        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n   272\t    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n   273\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n   274\t    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n   275\t    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n   276\t    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n   277\t    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   278\t    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n   279\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   280\t                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   281\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n   282\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   283\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   284\t    if errors:\n   285\t        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n   286\t    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n     1\t\"\"\"Preflight: run every code check and every prompt against the stored model answers before a paid run ($0).\n     2\t\n     3\tAGENTS.md §3 \"Strictness is code too\" and §4 \"a check must judge something\": a check is accepted on real data,\n     4\treports how many cases it judged, and a check over an empty population is unexercised. This script replays what\n     5\tthe archive and the earlier runs' views databases already hold through the current code and prints, per check,\n     6\tthe cases judged, the cases refused and the reasons with examples:\n     7\t\n     8\t  A. answers the schema refused (prompt and schema disagree: a value the prompt's wording suggested but the enum lacks)\n     9\t  B. extraction's code checks (extraction.sift) over every stored extraction answer\n    10\t  C. matching's code checks (matching.check) over every stored matching record, with the lists shown at the time\n    11\t  D. every schema enum value appears verbatim in the prompt that asks for it\n    12\t\n    13\tIt replays the answers of the versions the code builds (extraction v74i, judging-v7); a row of a retired version, or one whose\n    14\tconfiguration file is gone, is counted as not replayed and named. Usage: python3 scripts/preflight.py [--archive A] [--items I]\n    15\t[--views DB ...] (defaults: draw 1 of the frozen v108 run, poc/data/e2e-r9-frozen-v108-2026-11-03/d1, and the NVDA items database).\n    16\tExit status 1 when a check judged no case.\n    17\t\"\"\"\n    18\timport argparse\n    19\timport collections\n    20\timport glob\n    21\timport json\n    22\timport os\n    23\timport re\n    24\timport shutil\n    25\timport sqlite3\n    26\timport sys\n    27\timport tempfile\n    28\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    29\t\n    30\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n    31\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\n    32\tfrom hivemind import config, extraction, live_lock, model, testdb, universe, vocabulary  # noqa: E402\n    33\tfrom hivemind.views import judging, matching  # noqa: E402\n    34\t\n    35\tSCHEMAS = {'extract': extraction.schema_for(extraction.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS[0]), 'match': matching.SCHEMA, 'judge': judging.schema_for(judging.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS[0])}\n    36\t# the stored requests of both prompt languages (D163): Chinese headers up to extraction v5 / matching-v1, English from v6 / matching-v2\n    37\tITEM_ID = re.compile(r'【信息】编号 (\\S+?)，类别 |\\[Item\\] id (\\S+?), category ')\n    38\tMATCH_SHOWN = re.compile(r'^· (v\\d+)\\s?[（(]', re.M)\n    39\tJEV_ASKED = re.compile(r'\\b(v\\d+): ')          # a Jev candidate reason names every thesis it was asked about: 'jev: v1: different 0.55; …'\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef normalise_reason(text):\n    43\t    text = re.sub(r\"'[^']*'\", \"'…'\", text)\n    44\t    text = re.sub(r'\\[\\d+\\]', '[]', text)\n    45\t    text = re.sub(r'\\b[ev]\\d+\\b|\\bc\\d+\\b', '#', text)\n    46\t    text = re.sub(r'\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}', 'DATE', text)\n    47\t    return text[:90]\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\tdef tally(title, judged, refused, reasons, examples):\n    51\t    share = f'{refused / judged:.0%}' if judged else 'n/a'\n    52\t    print(f'\\n== {title}: judged {judged}, refused/dropped {refused} ({share})')\n    53\t    for reason, count in reasons.most_common(20):\n    54\t        print(f'   {count:5d}  {reason}')\n    55\t        for example in examples.get(reason, [])[:2]:\n    56\t            print(f'          e.g. {example}')\n    57\t\n    58\t\n    59\tdef part_a(archive_conn):\n    60\t    reasons, examples, judged = collections.Counter(), collections.defaultdict(list), 0\n    61\t    rows = archive_conn.execute(\"select purpose, request_sha256, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:schema:%' or request_sha256 like '%:malformed:%' or request_sha256 like '%:refused:%'\")\n    62\t    for purpose, sha, answer_json in (tuple(r) for r in rows):\n    63\t        judged += 1\n    64\t        if ':malformed:' in sha or not answer_json:\n    65\t            reasons[f'{purpose}: not JSON'] += 1\n    66\t            continue\n    67\t        for error in model.check_schema(json.loads(answer_json), SCHEMAS.get(purpose, {})):\n    68\t            key = f'{purpose}: {normalise_reason(error)}'\n    69\t            reasons[key] += 1\n    70\t            examples[key].append(error[:140])\n    71\t    tally('A. answers the schema refused (prompt/schema disagreements; empty when the provider enforces the schema server-side)', judged, judged, reasons, examples)\n    72\t    return judged\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\tclass Unverifiable(Exception):\n    76\t    \"\"\"A stored request of a retired version, or whose configuration file is gone: counted and named in the output, not replayed,\n    77\t    and not a failure of the archive.\"\"\"\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef _preflight_extract_inputs(request, item, cfg):\n    81\t    \"\"\"Validate the stored source and recover exactly the question ids production showed (its [Open questions] block).\"\"\"\n    82\t    setting = cfg.extraction_setting(item['category'])\n    83\t    version = setting.prompt_version.rpartition('-')[2]\n    84\t    if version not in extraction.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\n    85\t        raise Unverifiable(f'extraction {version} (retired)')\n    86\t    text = (item['text'] or '')[:extraction.MAX_TEXT_CHARS]          # production sends the first MAX_TEXT_CHARS characters\n    87\t    user = next(m['content'] for m in request['messages'] if m['role'] == 'user')\n    88\t    header = extraction.item_header(item, item['category'])\n    89\t    if user.count(header) != 1:\n    90\t        raise ValueError('source metadata does not match archived request')\n    91\t    before, after = user.split(header, 1)\n    92\t    if not after.startswith(text + '\\n\\n' + extraction.CLOSING):\n    93\t        raise ValueError('source text does not match archived request')\n    94\t    blocks = before.split('\\n\\n')\n    95\t    questions = [b for b in blocks if b.startswith('[Open questions at the start of ')]\n    96\t    if len(questions) != 1 or [b for b in blocks if b.startswith('[Research groups]')] != [extraction.GROUPS_INSTRUCTION]:\n    97\t        raise ValueError('unidentifiable open-questions or research-groups block')\n    98\t    view_ids = re.findall(r'^  - (v\\d+) \\(', questions[0], re.M)\n    99\t    if not view_ids and not questions[0].endswith('\\n  None yet.'):\n   100\t        raise ValueError('empty open-questions block lacks the empty marker')\n   101\t    if request['response_format']['json_schema']['schema'] != extraction.schema_for(version):\n   102\t        raise ValueError('archived schema does not match the configuration')\n   103\t    return version, view_ids\n   104\t\n   105\t\n   106\tdef part_b(archive_conn, items_conn, uni):\n   276\tdef part_d():\n   277\t    \"\"\"Every schema enum value appears in the prompt that asks for it: the extraction role and the judging prompt of the versions the\n   278\t    code builds, and every matching prompt against its own version's set (Chinese up to matching-v1, English after).\"\"\"\n   279\t    missing = []\n   280\t    checks = [(f'role-{v}.txt', extraction.TIERS + vocabulary.KINDS + vocabulary.ASSET_LABELS) for v in extraction.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS]\n   281\t    checks += [(f'{v}.txt', judging.PUSHES) for v in judging.SUPPORTED_VERSIONS]\n   282\t    for path in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(config.PROMPTS, 'matching-v*.txt'))):\n   283\t        version = os.path.basename(path).removesuffix('.txt')\n   284\t        checks.append((os.path.basename(path), (matching.OUTCOMES + matching.EVIDENCE_OUTCOMES + vocabulary.DIRECTIONS) if matching.is_english(version)\n   285\t                       else (matching.LEGACY_OUTCOMES + matching.LEGACY_EVIDENCE_OUTCOMES)))\n   286\t    judged = 0\n   287\t    for name, values in checks:\n   288\t        text = open(os.path.join(config.PROMPTS, name), encoding='utf-8').read()\n   289\t        for value in values:\n   290\t            judged += 1\n   291\t            if value not in text:\n   292\t                missing.append(f'{name} lacks the enum value {value!r}')\n   293\t    print(f'\\n== D. schema enum values named in the prompts: judged {judged}, missing {len(missing)}')\n   294\t    for line in missing:\n   295\t        print('   ', line)\n   296\t    return judged\n   297\t\n   298\t\n   299\tdef part_e(views_paths):\n   300\t    \"\"\"Keyed ledgers (keyed-views-plan.md 5): how many open views carry a key, how many keys collide among open views (the\n   301\t    pipeline's identity rule says none should), and what the watch list sent to the review pool. A ledger written before\n   302\t    keys is reported as unkeyed, not failed.\"\"\"\n   303\t    judged = 0\n   304\t    for path in views_paths:\n   305\t        conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   306\t        conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n   307\t        tables = {r[0] for r in conn.execute(\"select name from sqlite_master where type='table'\")}\n   308\t        if 'view_keys' not in tables:\n   309\t            print(f'\\n== E. keyed views in {os.path.basename(path)}: unkeyed ledger (written before keys)')\n   310\t            continue\n   311\t        open_ids = {r[0] for r in conn.execute('select view_id from view_switches where id in (select max(id) from view_switches group by view_id) and open=1')}\n   312\t        keys = collections.defaultdict(list)\n   313\t        for r in conn.execute('select k.*, v.object_id from view_keys k join views v on v.view_id=k.view_id'):\n   314\t            if r['view_id'] in open_ids:\n   315\t                keys[(r['object_id'], r['measure'], r['scope_key'], r['period_start'], r['period_end'], r['basis'], r['unit'], r['event_type'])].append(r['view_id'])\n   316\t        keyed = sum(len(v) for v in keys.values())\n   317\t        collisions = {k: v for k, v in keys.items() if len(v) > 1}\n   318\t        pool = conn.execute(\"select count(*) from review_pool_entries where kind='candidate_outside_watch'\").fetchone()[0]\n   319\t        judged += keyed\n   320\t        print(f'\\n== E. keyed views in {os.path.basename(path)}: open views {len(open_ids)}, keyed {keyed}, duplicate keys {len(collisions)} groups, review pool {pool} candidates outside the watch list')\n   321\t        for k, v in list(collisions.items())[:10]:\n   322\t            print(f'      {k[:3]} {k[3]}..{k[4]} → {v}')\n   323\t    return judged\n   324\t\n   325\t\n   326\tdef main():\n   327\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   328\t    frozen_draw = os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'e2e-r9-frozen-v108-2026-11-03', 'd1')\n   329\t    parser.add_argument('--archive', default=os.path.join(frozen_draw, 'archive.sqlite'))\n   330\t    parser.add_argument('--items', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'data', 'items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'))\n   331\t    parser.add_argument('--views', nargs='*', default=None)\n   332\t    parser.add_argument('--universe', default=os.path.join(ROOT, 'poc', 'universe.json'))\n   333\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n   334\t    views_paths = args.views or [os.path.join(frozen_draw, 'views.sqlite')]\n   335\t    archive_conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{args.archive}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n   336\t    archive_conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n   337\t    items_conn = testdb.open_db(args.items)\n   338\t    uni = universe.load(args.universe)\n   339\t    print('preflight over', args.archive, 'and', len(views_paths), 'views databases:', ', '.join(os.path.basename(os.path.dirname(p)) for p in views_paths))\n   340\t    part_a(archive_conn)\n   341\t    copies = store_copies(views_paths)\n   342\t    counts = [part_b(archive_conn, items_conn, uni), part_c(archive_conn, copies, uni), part_d()]\n   343\t    part_e(copies)          # informational for unkeyed ledgers; judged counts are reported per ledger\n   344\t    if min(counts) == 0:\n   345\t        print('\\nUNEXERCISED: a check judged no case')\n   346\t        sys.exit(1)\n   347\t    print('\\npreflight done')\n   348\t\n   349\t\n   350\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   351\t    main()\n    60\t    if not isinstance(answers, dict) or set(answers) != set(questions):\n    61\t        return ['answer set differs from the questions asked']\n    62\t    for qid, question in questions.items():\n    63\t        answer = answers[qid]\n    64\t        if not isinstance(answer, dict) or answer.get('type') != question['type']:\n    65\t            problems.append(f'{qid}: answer type mismatch')\n    66\t            continue\n    67\t        if question['type'] == 'noul':\n    68\t            if not isinstance(answer.get('noul'), (int, float)) or not 0 <= answer['noul'] <= 1:\n    69\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: noul out of range')\n    70\t        elif question['type'] == 'choice':\n    71\t            probabilities = answer.get('probabilities')\n    72\t            if answer.get('choice') not in question['criteria'] or not isinstance(probabilities, dict) or set(probabilities) != set(question['criteria']):\n    73\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: choice or probabilities do not match the criteria')\n    74\t            elif any(not isinstance(v, (int, float)) or isinstance(v, bool) or not 0 <= v <= 1 for v in probabilities.values()) \\\n    75\t                    or abs(sum(probabilities.values()) - 1) > 0.005 * len(probabilities) + 1e-9:\n    76\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: probabilities are not a distribution')\n    77\t            elif probabilities[answer['choice']] < max(probabilities.values()) - ROUNDING - 1e-9:\n    78\t                problems.append(f'{qid}: choice is not the most probable option')\n    79\t    return problems\n    80\t\n    81\t\n    82\tdef request_for(setting, state, questions):\n    83\t    \"\"\"The complete Jev request used both for dispatch and in-flight identity.\"\"\"\n    84\t    return {'model': setting.model, 'state': state, 'questions': questions}\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef ask(archive, cfg, setting, state, questions, purpose, *, transport=None):\n    88\t    \"\"\"One Jev request, archived; returns model.Answer whose data is the `answers` map.\"\"\"\n    89\t    request = request_for(setting, state, questions)\n    90\t    request_json, sha = model.request_identity(request)\n    91\t    prompt_chars = len(request_json)\n    92\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n    93\t    if hit:\n    94\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n    95\t        return model.Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n    96\t    started = time.time()\n    97\t    response = (transport or globals()['transport'])(request)\n    98\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 2)\n    99\t    answers = response.get('answers') if isinstance(response, dict) else None\n   100\t    problems = validate(answers, questions)\n   101\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {} if isinstance(response, dict) else {}\n   102\t    input_tokens, output_tokens = int(usage.get('input_tokens') or 0), int(usage.get('output_tokens') or 0)\n   103\t    price_in, _ = model.PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   104\t    cost = round(input_tokens / 1e6 * price_in, 6)\n   105\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   106\t                             request_sha256=sha if not problems else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   107\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response, ensure_ascii=False)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(answers, ensure_ascii=False) if answers is not None else None,\n   108\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   109\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   110\t    if problems:\n   111\t        raise model.SchemaError('; '.join(problems[:5]))\n   112\t    return model.Answer(answers, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\nscripts/preflight.py:61:    rows = archive_conn.execute(\"select purpose, request_sha256, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256 like '%:schema:%' or request_sha256 like '%:malformed:%' or request_sha256 like '%:refused:%'\")\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:344:                archive.retire(answer.call_id)                 # a refused answer never answers the same request again (a resume re-samples)\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:348:                    archive.retire(answer.call_id)\nsrc/hivemind/jev.py:106:                             request_sha256=sha if not problems else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:99:            self.conn.execute(\"update model_calls set request_sha256 = request_sha256 || ':refused:' || ? where call_id=? and request_sha256 not like '%:refused:%'\",\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:268:                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\nsrc/hivemind/model.py:280:                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
